course: dictionary
lesson: 8554
title: Scandal: more than gossip
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A scandal is something wrong or shameful that people find out about, and it shocks them. «Some years ago some British newspaper journalists secretly listened to famous people's phone messages, which is against the law; they were caught, and it became a huge scandal.» Secretly listening to people's messages is wrong, and when people found out, they were shocked. That is a scandal.
explain: Use the context to check. «Famous people still buy chocolate, rewear dresses and get haircuts; none of that is a scandal.» Buying chocolate is not wrong or shameful, so nobody is shocked by it. Ask yourself: is this wrong, and would people be shocked to find out? If not, it is not a scandal.
explain: Scandal can also mean the talk and gossip about a shameful thing. It can also be used with a feeling of "that is unfair!" «The Leopard grumbled, "This daylight hunting is a perfect scandal".» The Leopard is not talking about a secret. He thinks the hunting is very unfair and wrong.
fact: A scandal is something wrong or shameful that people find out about and are shocked by.
fact: Scandal can also mean the gossip and talk about such things.
fact: In everyday speech, «It's a scandal» means something is very unfair or wrong.
fact: «Scandal» is often used in news about famous people, such as someone who lied or cheated.
fact: News about a scandal can be loud, and some details may be rumours, so check carefully.
exercise: «Some newspaper journalists secretly listened to famous people's phone messages, and it became a huge scandal.» What is a scandal here? | A happy party for famous people | A new kind of phone | A type of chocolate | *Something shameful that people found out about and were shocked by
exercise: «Famous people still buy chocolate, rewear dresses and get haircuts; none of that is a scandal.» Why is buying chocolate not a scandal? | It is against the law | It is famous, so it is a scandal | *It is not wrong or shameful, so nobody is shocked by it | It is always shocking
exercise: Mia says, "It's a scandal that the park is closed on our birthday!" What does she mean? | She is going to the park | The park is very big | *Something is very unfair
test: A scandal is something wrong or shameful that people find out about. Which one is a scandal? | *A famous person who lied and was caught | A cup of tea | A bridge built on time | A sunny day
test: The news talked about the scandal all week, with loud gossip. What does scandal mean here? | *Gossip and talk about a shameful thing | A quiet walk in the park | A dance | A new kind of food
exam: In «The Leopard grumbled, "This daylight hunting is a perfect scandal"», what does the Leopard mean? | The hunting is very tasty | *The hunting is very unfair and wrong | The Leopard is happy and dancing | The hunting is in the dark
